{
  "title": "Frastown West Berth image-to-3D review",
  "operator_intent": "Generate an isolated asset image, reconstruct on the local GPU, and run the RAC gates before replacing a scene proxy. Preserve dry detail for VR; add rain and wetness at scene level.",
  "workflow": {
    "image": "ComfyUI / Z-Image Turbo, immutable PNG, seed, graph, prompt ID and SHA-256",
    "geometry": "RAC run_hy3d_geometry.ps1 / Hunyuan3D-2, primary reference locked by SHA-256",
    "paint": "RAC prepare_texture_uv_transport.py, then run_hy3d21_texture.ps1, studio 4096 PNG"
  },
  "findings": {
    "CT-02.1": "The first mesh retained a skirt and opened a false hole through one pier. The separately hashed v02 reference removes the floor shadow. The reconstructed v02 front, side and reverse show a clean base, continuous return and open recess. A 36,000-triangle UV transport passed. Paint and world fit are separate review gates.",
    "DK-01.1": "The view-conditioned mesh has a continuous hull and visible deck. Confirm the 15 m centreline, 5 m beam, separate gunwale, level deck and gangway lip before using it as the player floor. The inferred wood deck finish still needs the dark steel specified in the brief.",
    "PR-02.1": "The GPU clay reconstruction has a coherent patch and free edge. Keep the wall mount at local zero. Review woven grain, frame separation and underside seams under close-up light before production approval.",
    "WK-07.2": "The conditioned mesh has an unintended bend. Compare straight lane, coplanar hinge and bearing ends at a full 3.00 m span before paint.",
    "CT-05.2": "One-view reconstruction filled key negative spaces. Test the entry opening and open iron lattice before paint.",
    "DK-03.1": "The launch geometry followed the overall silhouette but retained an extra extension beside the bolted base. Review from both sides before snapping it to the deck.",
    "AC-04.1": "An empty interior and rim are visible in reconstructed geometry. The first painted bowl showed triangular artifacts around the rim. Review the repainted interior and 0.22 m cover fit before attaching any hand socket.",
    "CT-03.2": "The door, handle, lintel and sash reconstruct clearly. The candidate is a front panel; use a separate structural wall return and test the opening against the gallery datum.",
    "CT-05.1": "The first mesh retains open bracing and a readable upper landing. Add the shaft interfaces and check the headhouse enclosure and clearance above the cage.",
    "CT-09.1": "Dry brick relief and hollow arch are readable. The first revision captures a studio-floor skirt, so retain the staged proxy while revising the image mask.",
    "PR-01.1": "The workbench silhouette, vise and trestles appear on two sides. Check that the top stays level and the vise clears the mechanic’s hands.",
    "PR-01.2": "The tools remain distinct on the panel, with extra backdrop geometry behind and below it. Clean the image silhouette and reconstruct before fitting the wall mount.",
    "PR-01.3": "The 3D mesh retains the two patched wings, tail and thin rigging. Inspect the underside and hanging pivot before paint and placement."
  },
  "pipeline_feedback": [
    "The optional -DiagnosticsDir flag is accepted by the PowerShell wrapper and rejected by the selected hash-pinned studio runner. Status should say which runner supports each option before consuming a GPU slot.",
    "The studio painter expects topology-locked UVs. The raw geometry GLB correctly has no UVs and caused a ColorVisuals.uv exception. Feed the RAC UV transport OBJ and surface-check receipt into studio paint; fail clearly when a source has no UVs.",
    "The first awning atlas used 9.44% of UV area. Decimated GLB flat normals had split nearly every triangle into separate vertices. Exporting the connected geometry without split normals gave 13,996 vertices, carried all 28,000 triangles, and used 60.79% of the UV area. Track atlas occupancy plus connectedness and inspect at hand distance before approving even a 4096 map.",
    "The first three 4K paint jobs wrote GLB, OBJ, lossless base color, roughness and metallic maps, and valid geometry/UV receipts before the subprocess exited with Windows code -1073741819. Record subprocess health separately from the artifact gate and retain both.",
    "Large architectural modules need a silhouette gate from front, back, side and above. A matching hero-camera still can miss a blocked aperture, a bent connector, or the studio floor leaking into 3D.",
    "Framewright should distinguish exact steel masters, image authorities, raw clay candidates, painted candidates, and placement proxies. A production status requires physical bounds, pivot evidence and a human-scale review.",
    "The prior 100× scale correction remains applicable: use metre-authored scene coordinates, apply centimetres to signed render and UCX bounds for Unreal and verify the imported 200 cm control span with its sockets."
  ],
